From: Yi Xie <imxieyi@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 16:36:57 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] Embedding: a misaligned CMPXCHG16B raises #GP

CMPXCHG16B requires a 16-byte aligned operand and raises #GP(0) for
any other, locked or not, before it reads or writes memory, as a Xeon
does. FEXCore emulated the misaligned exchange; an embedding host now
gets the fault through EmbedderRequireAlignment.
---
 FEXCore/Source/Interface/Core/OpcodeDispatcher.cpp | 6 ++++++
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+)

diff --git a/FEXCore/Source/Interface/Core/OpcodeDispatcher.cpp b/FEXCore/Source/Interface/Core/OpcodeDispatcher.cpp
index 1b18e4b26e458de570a3bcad25f8cca1bcc37f13..56c024fdc19507f412f2b8b3072023adf4133230 100644
--- a/FEXCore/Source/Interface/Core/OpcodeDispatcher.cpp
+++ b/FEXCore/Source/Interface/Core/OpcodeDispatcher.cpp
@@ -4261,6 +4261,12 @@ void OpDispatchBuilder::CMPXCHGPairOp(OpcodeArgs) {
 
   HandledLock = (Op->Flags & FEXCore::X86Tables::DecodeFlags::FLAG_LOCK) != 0;
 
+  // CMPXCHG16B raises #GP for an operand that is not 16-byte aligned, before
+  // it reads anything.
+  if (Size == OpSize::i64Bit) {
+    EmbedderRequireAlignment(Op, MakeSegmentAddress(Op, Op->Dest), 16);
+  }
+
   // If this is a memory location then we want the pointer to it
   Ref Src1 = MakeSegmentAddress(Op, Op->Dest);
 
